<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 3.0 pct in October - Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 3.0 pct in October - Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	   OCT 96    SEPT 96   (OCT 95)</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.1	  0.3	(0.5)</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     3.0	  3.4	(5.8)</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    104.5	104.4    (115.8)</p>
<p>Note: The 1996 data is based on a new basket of goods. The 1995 data was collated under an old basket.</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 3.0 percent for October.  </p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)     104.7	   -0.4	    +3.3</p>
<p> Clothing			 105.4	   +1.0	    +3.6</p>
<p> Housing, Electricity,Fuel  105.9	   +1.3	    +4.0</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 104.2	   +0.1	    +2.9</p>
<p> Health spending		102.6	   +0.2	    +1.9</p>
<p> Transport			105.0	   -0.4	    +3.1</p>
<p> Recreation		     103.5	   -0.1	    +2.5</p>
<p> Education			105.3	   +0.6	    +1.4</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  104.7	   +0.1	    +3.5</p>
<p> Other goods,services	 103.0	   -0.1	    +1.6</p>
<p>(including communications)</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
